    <string name="footer_help">Audio is sent as raw PCM over UDP on your local network only — no cloud, no accounts, no analytics. Playback uses normal media routing, so the audio goes wherever Android sends media: your paired hearing aids, Bluetooth headphones or the phone speaker.\n\nKeep the phone and the TV box on the same Wi-Fi network. 5 GHz is preferable to 2.4 GHz for lower latency and less packet loss.</string>
